From fe0c04077b7b53b48c3529e614743e83ba357309 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 15:37:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Use harmonic evidence to pick tactus; preserve cancellation
 and enforce decode cap

### Motivation

- Prevent octave errors where onset peaks select a double-time tempo instead of the musical tactus by incorporating harmonic and bar-level evidence.
- Preserve coroutine cancellation semantics when probing and decoding media so user-initiated cancels are not swallowed and misreported as failures.
- Enforce the decoded-duration cap inside codec buffer consumption to avoid holding excess audio and unnecessary memory pressure.

### Description

- Add `MetricalHypothesisEvaluator` which scores tempo/meter/downbeat hypotheses using onset support, beat fit, accent contrast, harmonic-change alignment, and bar-level chroma repetition.
- Integrate the evaluator into `AudioAnalyzer.analyzeRhythm` and pass the selected tempo to `TempoEstimator.curve`; carry the selected `beatsPerMeasure` into structure estimation via `analyzeStructure`.
- Change `TempoEstimator.curve` signature to accept an `anchorBpm` so the windowed tempo path is anchored to the chosen metrical level.
- Stop consuming a codec output buffer as soon as the sink reaches the configured `maxOutputSamples` by guarding `DecodeSink.append` with `!isFull`.
- Rethrow `CancellationException` in `PcmDecoder.decode`, `MediaProbe.probe`, and `MediaProbe.checksum` so coroutine cancellation is not converted into ordinary failures.
- Ensure `LibraryViewModel.onImport` clears the `importing` flag in a `finally` block so the UI cannot remain stuck importing after an error or cancellation.
- Add unit tests: new harmonic-rhythm cases in `AudioAnalyzerTest` and a decode-cap test in `DecodeSinkTest`, and add an audit report document.

### Testing

- No Gradle/JVM unit tests were executed in this environment because the Android SDK and required uncached artifacts were unavailable; please run the JVM tests in CI with `./gradlew :core:audio:test` and related tasks for verification.
- New unit tests added are `AudioAnalyzerTest` cases for harmonic-tactus selection and `DecodeSinkTest` for the decode cap and are expected to validate the new behavior once run in CI.
- The repository audit script ran host Python checks (unrelated training tests) which passed in this environment, but Android/Gradle verification must be performed in CI.
